{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-103310",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The period of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-11$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+(-11)\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-11\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{5}{4},$ we get that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-11\\pi )=\\frac{5}{4}.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n24\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-11\\pi )-3=24(\\frac{5}{4})-3=30-3=27.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
